   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the town law, in relation to town justices of the town of Rye\nfollowing the dissolution of the Port Chester village court",
    "basePrintNo": "S4945",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S4945-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §20, Town L",
    "lawSection": "Town Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S4945\n\nSPONSOR: MAYER\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the town law, in relation to town justices of the town\nof Rye following the dissolution of the Port Chester village court\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nTo amend the Town Law to authorize the Rye town court to have two addi-\ntional justices.\n\n \nSUMMARY PROVISIONS:\n\nThis bill would :\n\n   *authorize the Town of Rye to elect two additional justices if the\nVillage of Port Chester abolishes its court May 15, 2021;\n\n   *transfer all village court actions and proceedings to the Rye town\ncourt;\n\n   *ensure the Village retains the authority to re-establish a village\ncourt and the Town retains the ability to abolish the two additional\njustice positions;\n\n   *authorize the Town to appoint two interim justices until elections\ntake place; and,\n\n   *allow the Town to initially elect one of the new justice positions\nto an initial two-year term to ensure that no more than two justices are\nup for election in the same year.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis legislation has been requested by the Town of Rye to facilitate the\ntown's assumption of court responsibilities handled by the village of\nPort Chester. The village has voted to dissolve the village court with\nthat dissolution to take effect on May 15, 2021.  The village court has\nbeen responsible for a busy caseload that necessitates adding justices\nto the town court to accommodate the level of activity the town court\nwill receive. The town has carefully reviewed the anticipated workload.\nThis request matches that analysis. With the dissolution of the village\ncourt and expansion of the town court the result will be a reduction of\none full local justice position.\n\nTo allow for the transition to meet the May 15, 2021 dissolution, the\nlegislation allows for appointment of acting justices by the town until\njustices can be elected at the next general election this November and\nfor an initial 2-year term for one of the new positions to rationalize\nthe town's justice terms going forward.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nTo be determined\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately and shall have been deemed to\nhave been in full force and effect on and after October 5, 2020.\n",
